# records/ holds raw transcripts: workspace-local evidence, not project
# documentation. P08 depends on RED-baseline.md, which IS committed, so a
# different workspace loses nothing that matters. This rule is permanent --
# unlike the oracles.md rule that stood here while P01 was measuring, which
# P01's final task removed on the way out. See
# tests/test_oracle_disclosure_order.py for why the order mattered.
records/

# RECORD-TEMPLATE.md is the scaffold a raw record is copied from. Like
# records/ it is workspace-local and PERMANENTLY ignored -- no phase commits
# it, so unlike the oracles.md rule that stood above it, this one has no
# expiry and must not be removed now that P01 has closed. Without this line
# the template is an untracked file one `git add -A` away from the repository,
# and it breaks the empty `git status --short` every task in this phase gates
# on.
# tests/test_record_template_ignored.py enforces it.
RECORD-TEMPLATE.md

# scoring.md is Task 9 working output: verbatim rationalizations plus the
# oracle predicates they were scored against. Same secrecy as oracles.md while
# P01 measures, and unlike oracles.md no phase ever commits it — Task 10
# curates RED-baseline.md from it, which IS committed.
scoring.md
